A person who normally works for themselves in one country and then goes to do the same kind of work in another country is still followed by the rules of the first country, as long as the time spent there is short. If you run your business in two or more countries:  
(a) you follow the country where you live if you do most of your work there;  
(b) if you do not live in one country, you follow the rules of the country where your main business happens. If you work for someone in one or more countries and also run your own business in another, the country where you work for someone decides the rules. If you work for someone in two or more countries, we use the first rule about which country applies.

